# Line endings are part of this project's correctness, not a style preference.
#
# contracts/cachet.py is hashed and compared against what is deployed on chain.
# With git left to its own devices that comparison is platform dependent:
# core.autocrlf rewrites the file to CRLF on a Windows checkout and LF
# everywhere else, so the same commit produces two different digests and a
# check that is meant to prove "the deployed bytes are the source" fails for
# half the people who run it.
#
# Everything is therefore stored and checked out with LF, on every machine.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary. Never touched, never normalised.
*.woff2 binary
*.woff binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary
*.mp4 binary
*.pdf binary
